1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:08,440
An assistant saying done is not proof. AIGON PROOF gives each action an exact review,

2
00:00:08,440 --> 00:00:13,514
an authenticated approval, and a receipt for the work actually performed.

3
00:00:14,258 --> 00:00:20,086
First, a client contract is addressed to an external partner. The server knows the

4
00:00:20,086 --> 00:00:26,239
document contains personal data. It blocks the action. Even an operator cannot

5
00:00:26,239 --> 00:00:28,190
approve this policy violation.

6
00:00:28,933 --> 00:00:35,051
We explicitly choose the anonymised summary instead. The document and recipient are

7
00:00:35,051 --> 00:00:40,973
shown before approval. Nothing in this command invents consent or silently changes

8
00:00:40,973 --> 00:00:42,447
the trust boundary.

9
00:00:43,191 --> 00:00:48,891
The operator unlocks approval with a private credential. That credential is never

10
00:00:48,891 --> 00:00:52,107
part of the agent's command or passport.

11
00:00:52,851 --> 00:00:59,236
Approve once records who approved the exact action fingerprint. The server now signs

12
00:00:59,236 --> 00:01:04,832
a short-lived passport. This is permission, not a delivery claim.

13
00:01:05,567 --> 00:01:11,070
Changing the recipient invalidates the authorization. The original approved action

14
00:01:11,070 --> 00:01:13,137
remains available to execute.

15
00:01:13,869 --> 00:01:19,105
Execute performs the work. The server writes actual document bytes into the

16
00:01:19,105 --> 00:01:26,861
recipient's local inbox, reads them back, verifies their SHA-256 hash, and persists

17
00:01:26,861 --> 00:01:27,755
this receipt.

18
00:01:28,492 --> 00:01:34,912
A second execution is rejected. One human approval cannot be reused through another

19
00:01:34,912 --> 00:01:36,247
passport either.

20
00:01:36,976 --> 00:01:42,421
After restarting the server, the receipt history is still here. Approval and replay

21
00:01:42,421 --> 00:01:46,310
records are durable, not just browser state.

22
00:01:47,054 --> 00:01:52,871
The operator can also deny or revoke an action. A denial does not produce a usable

23
00:01:52,871 --> 00:01:53,788
passport.

24
00:01:54,520 --> 00:02:00,789
Six negative policy probes check forged approval, sensitive egress and unknown

25
00:02:00,789 --> 00:02:07,012
parameters. The demonstration also exercises real recipient tampering and replay.

26
00:02:07,759 --> 00:02:17,674
The same Rust service exposes the governance explorer and MCP protocol 2025-11-25.

27
00:02:17,674 --> 00:02:22,295
AIGON PROOF: approve the action, verify the outcome.
